graph timeline
rows timeline context detail
base Discovery

state Discovery [timeline]:
  text:
    Interview the people with the problem and name the assumption most likely to kill the project.
  next -> Prototype

state Prototype [timeline]:
  text:
    Build the smallest complete interaction that can test the central claim with real users.
  next -> Pilot

state Pilot [timeline]:
  text:
    Run the process at limited scale and measure failures, recovery time, and operator load.
  next -> Release

state Release [timeline]:
  text:
    Expand only after the pilot survives its acceptance criteria and the support path is staffed.

state Problem frame [context]:
  text:
    The project exists to shorten a handoff that currently loses decisions between teams.
  develops -> Test cohort
  explains -> Discovery

state Test cohort [context]:
  text:
    Five operators use the prototype on representative work before the implementation hardens.
  develops -> Acceptance gate
  explains -> Prototype

state Acceptance gate [context]:
  text:
    The pilot must complete twenty runs without an unrecoverable handoff or silent data loss.
  governs -> Pilot

state Threat model [detail]:
  text:
    Enumerate the failures that could expose data, stall the process, or hide a bad handoff.
  develops -> Security review
  informs -> Pilot

state Security review [detail]:
  text:
    Access review and incident ownership must close before the release decision.
  blocks -> Release
